      "side": 1,
      "message": "When a rule author writes `attr.label(default\u003dNone)`, `AttrSchema::create` calls `create_without_defaults` before `schema.default` has been populated. This branch therefore treats the `None` as mandatory and returns `MandatoryAttribute`, even though omitting the default creates the same optional `Attr::Label(None)`.\n\nI\u0027d argue that the two should be equivalent from a user perspective (and I think that\u0027s what Bazel does, but admittedly haven\u0027t tested it).",
      "revId": "67a01027d8467b6bc48d2550a7bc8f22818cfdcd",
