      "writtenOn": "2026-07-06T02:54:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The macro body expands bare `use std::fmt;`, `use starlark::values::Value;`, `use starlark::values::none::NoneOr;`, etc. at the invocation site.\n\n`macro_rules!` does not hygienically isolate imports, so the first real caller that invokes this in a module already containing `use starlark::values::Value;`, or invokes the macro twice, gets \"error[E0252]: the name Value is defined multiple times\".",
      "revId": "67a01027d8467b6bc48d2550a7bc8f22818cfdcd",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
